# interplay_memlive_migrate_protocol: A guest moving three objects' pages the way that works in every setup, checked against a control task that never moves them. Both tasks fill a shared buffer, a private buffer and a private heap's buffer with invalidateGuest and synchronize (6), so the guest pages hold the GPU's bytes; task 1 then copies each object into a helper buffer over a fresh page (the GPU copies the host copy), points the objects' leaves at the fresh pages, unmaps (34) the old VAs (the blocks setup's host task maps them again at their next use), discards the objects (63), and scribbles over the old pages, as a guest reusing them would. Both tasks then fill again and read everything out with invalidateHost: the two tasks' reads are equal in every setup (compared).
